\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When shall Thy love constrain,
\par And force me to Thy breast?
\par When shall my soul return again
\par To her eternal rest?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy condescending grace
\par To me did freely move;
\par It calls me still to seek Thy face,
\par And stoops to ask my love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord, at Thy feet I fall!
\par I long to be set free;
\par I fain would now obey the call,
\par And give up all for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To rescue me from woe,
\par Thou didst with all things part;
\par Didst lead a suffering life below,
\par To gain my worthless heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. My worthless heart to gain,
\par The God of all that breath
\par Was found in fashion as a man,
\par And died a cursed death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And can I yet delay
\par My little all to give?
\par To tear my soul from earth away,
\par For Jesus to receive?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Nay, but I yield, I yield!
\par I can hold out no more,
\par I sink, by dying love compelled,
\par And own Thee conqueror.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

